Subject: [PATCH 08140/11362] [outer-loop] CORRECTION: the placeholder-verdict
 claim in the .528 override was false

Commit 05a8f9b8a8 justified the exp5973 capstone operator_override on TWO grounds. The
first (CLAUDE.md class 1: capstone-vN scope-matches every prior capstone by construction
and reconciles its own milestone, so it cannot be a doomed rerun) is correct and is
independently sufficient. The SECOND was fabricated by a bad grep and is retracted.

I claimed exp5716 and exp5768 carried template-placeholder text in honest_verdict --
"terminal summary starting with complete: or blocked:." -- and that the linter's prior-
failure matches were therefore spurious. Both halves are false.

The extraction was `grep -o '"honest_verdict"[^,]*' results/experiment_NNNN_*.json | head -1`.
It failed twice over: it took the FIRST match in each file, which was a field DESCRIPTION
rather than the value, and the bare glob matched the wrong experiment entirely (the
experiment_5728_* glob returned cnn_weight_sweep, not the capstone).

Actual top-level verdicts, parsed properly:
  exp5716  blocked: v510 reconciled; exp5708_stream_promoted=False; ...
  exp5728  blocked: v511 reconciled; answer_channel_ready=false; ...
  exp5768  complete: V514 reconciled: bridges ready, ... ARC composition gate blocked
  exp5862  blocked: required capstone checks failed during V521 reconciliation
  exp5903  complete_with_nulls: all 14 activated .524 identities are terminal ...

All five are real, well-formed verdicts. THREE ARE GENUINELY blocked:, so the linter
counting them as prior failures is CORRECT. There is no placeholder-verdict defect, and
the "will keep manufacturing phantom prior-failures for every future capstone" prediction
built on it is withdrawn.

The override text carried this false claim into live project record read by the linter and
planner, so it is corrected in place with the retraction stated rather than silently
removed (never-prune). The unblock itself stands on the class-1 ground alone; .528
activated at 09:37 and the conductor is working.

